当时我就觉得，天哪，这事儿可能真的要成了。

334
00:13:41.540 --> 00:13:43.140
And it did.
结果真的成了。

335
00:13:43.400 --> 00:13:45.120
They bought it.
他们认可了我。

336
00:13:46.960 --> 00:13:51.580
And that it really, like, started everything for me.
这真的开启了我的一切。

337
00:13:51.760 --> 00:13:57.220
I got just instant cred getting to be a part of that show.
能参与那部剧，让我瞬间获得了认可。

338
00:13:57.220 --> 00:14:02.480
So, and I'm just like, what a fun, fun first role it was.
所以，我当时就想，这真是一个非常有趣的角色。

339
00:14:03.500 --> 00:14:04.240
So cool.
太酷了。

340
00:14:04.460 --> 00:14:06.600
You know, I hadn't watched this episode in a long time.
你知道，我很久没看这一集了。

341
00:14:06.640 --> 00:14:09.180
And when it got to that scene, I was like, oh, my God, there's Katie.
当看到那一幕时，我心想，天哪，是凯蒂。

342
00:14:09.680 --> 00:14:12.440
And she is so incredibly charming.
她真的非常有魅力。

343
00:14:12.760 --> 00:14:16.140
Like, I want her and Michael to date, you know?
我甚至希望她和迈克尔能约会，你懂吗？

344
00:14:16.340 --> 00:14:16.660
I know.
我懂。

345
00:14:16.860 --> 00:14:17.620
They're so cute.
他们太可爱了。

346
00:14:17.920 --> 00:14:18.760
Same, Angela.
我也这么觉得，安吉拉。

347
00:14:18.940 --> 00:14:20.900
When I saw it, I was like, oh, my gosh, it's Katie.
当我看到的时候，我也在想，天哪，是凯蒂。

348
00:14:21.420 --> 00:14:22.940
And she's an amazing actress.
她是一位了不起的演员。

349
00:14:23.320 --> 00:14:24.580
She's also a director.
她还是一位导演。

350
00:14:24.900 --> 00:14:26.300
She's directed three filMs.
她已经执导过三部电影了。

351
00:14:26.300 --> 00:14:30.620
Her latest film is starring Diane Keaton, Elizabeth Lale, and Nicole Byer.
她最近的一部电影由黛安·基顿、伊丽莎白·莱尔和妮可·拜尔主演。

352
00:14:30.740 --> 00:14:31.900
It's called Mac and Rita.
片名叫《麦克与丽塔》。

353
00:14:32.160 --> 00:14:33.980
She's in post-production on it now.
她现在正在进行后期制作。

354
00:14:34.120 --> 00:14:38.800
And I told her that when it comes out, we'll put a shout-out in the pod so that people can find it.
我告诉她，等电影上映时，我们会在播客里宣传一下，好让大家都能找到它。

355
00:14:38.960 --> 00:14:40.680
Yeah, that's a great caSt.
没错，那真是个很棒的演员阵容。

356
00:14:41.040 --> 00:14:44.640
Well, lady, that is all of my fast facts.
好了，女士，这就是我所有的快讯了。

357
00:14:45.040 --> 00:14:46.500
Well, I think we should go to break.
我觉得我们该休息一下了。

358
00:14:46.500 --> 00:14:50.200
Because when we come back, I might need to throw Jim a little shade.
因为等我们回来，我可能得损一下吉姆。

359
00:14:50.760 --> 00:14:51.220
Really?
真的吗？

360
00:14:51.540 --> 00:14:51.880
Yeah.
是的。

361
00:14:52.520 --> 00:14:54.160
I can't wait to find out why.
我迫不及待想知道原因了。

362
00:14:54.160 --> 00:14:56.940
I might have something tacky to say.
我可能有些刻薄的话要说。

363
00:14:57.140 --> 00:14:57.420
Oh.
哦。

364
00:14:58.120 --> 00:14:58.600
Oh.
哦。

365
00:14:58.860 --> 00:15:00.180
Those are always my favorite messages.
我最喜欢听那种话了。

366
00:15:00.480 --> 00:15:01.160
What do you mean?
你什么意思？

367
00:15:01.280 --> 00:15:03.760
You'll, like, text me and be like, hey, can you call me?
你会发短信给我说，嘿，能给我打个电话吗？

368
00:15:03.820 --> 00:15:05.060
I have something tacky to say.
我有刻薄的话要说。

369
00:15:05.700 --> 00:15:07.920
And I'm like, oh, I can't wait.
然后我就想，哦，我等不及了。

370
00:15:08.080 --> 00:15:09.160
I'm like, drop everything.
我就像，放下手头一切。

371
00:15:09.160 --> 00:15:10.440
I have to call Angela.
我得给安吉拉打电话。

372
00:15:11.200 --> 00:15:11.840
All right.
好吧。

373
00:15:11.920 --> 00:15:12.520
We'll be back.
我们马上回来。

374
00:15:22.520 --> 00:15:28.940
Angela, while you were getting tea during your break, Sam told me something beyond fascinating that I didn't know.
安吉拉，刚才休息时你去泡茶，山姆告诉我一件我不知道的、极其迷人的事。

375
00:15:29.120 --> 00:15:30.820
It's more news about blood.
是关于血液的更多消息。

376
00:15:31.120 --> 00:15:31.420
What?
什么？

377
00:15:31.420 --> 00:15:32.760
Sam, will you please share?
山姆，你能分享一下吗？

378
00:15:33.240 --> 00:15:36.820
Yeah, they have blood donors and banks, just like for humans, but for dogs.
好的，他们有献血者和血库，就像人类的一样，但这是给狗用的。

379
00:15:37.500 --> 00:15:37.900
Aw.
啊。

380
00:15:38.340 --> 00:15:39.660
And they do the same thing.
而且他们做的事情也一样。

381
00:15:39.760 --> 00:15:42.080
They donate little pouches of blood.
它们会捐献一小袋一小袋的血。

382
00:15:42.280 --> 00:15:45.840
And Sam got to meet a dog that donates his blood once a month at your vet.
山姆还在你们兽医那里见到了一只每月献血一次的狗。

383
00:15:45.840 --> 00:15:49.640
His name is Ben, and he's a golden retriever, and he has a little vest with a heart on it.
它叫本，是一只金毛寻回犬，穿着一件印有心形图案的小背心。

384
00:15:50.540 --> 00:15:51.200
Aw, Ben.
啊，本。

385
00:15:51.480 --> 00:15:53.100
And he's a very good boy.
它真是个好孩子。

386
00:15:53.480 --> 00:15:54.740
Oh, that is so sweet.
哦，那太贴心了。

387
00:15:54.800 --> 00:15:55.280
Very good boy.
真是个好孩子。

388
00:15:55.280 --> 00:15:56.900
That is, like, stuff I don't even think about.
这些事我甚至都没想过。

389
00:15:57.000 --> 00:15:57.280
I know.
我知道。

390
00:15:57.280 --> 00:15:57.860
But of course.
但理应如此。

391
00:15:58.100 --> 00:15:58.660
Of course.
当然。

392
00:15:59.200 --> 00:15:59.720
All right.
好了。

393
00:15:59.860 --> 00:16:00.680
Should we get started?
我们要开始了吗？

394
00:16:00.920 --> 00:16:02.060
Let's get started.
让我们开始吧。

395
00:16:02.820 --> 00:16:03.600
Guess what?
你猜怎么着？

396
00:16:03.800 --> 00:16:04.020
What?
什么？

397
00:16:04.020 --> 00:16:14.020
There is a rep from Techstar who says there's a whole new operating system for the phones, and he could, like, meet with Michael Scott, but Michael Scott's never around.
有个Techstar的代表说手机有一套全新的操作系统，他本来可以和迈克尔·斯科特见面的，但迈克尔·斯科特从来不在。

398
00:16:14.200 --> 00:16:14.880
I wonder why.
我好奇为什么。

399
00:16:15.580 --> 00:16:24.700
Well, Pam says if they get this new phone system that allows the caller to contact the salespeople directly, that's basically 95% of her job.
帕姆说，如果他们换了这套新电话系统，让来电者能直接联系销售人员，那基本上就占了她工作量的95%。

400
00:16:24.800 --> 00:16:29.980
So she is clearly never letting this guy meet Michael because she doesn't want to lose her job.
所以很明显，她绝不会让这家伙见到迈克尔，因为她不想丢掉工作。

401
00:16:30.140 --> 00:16:32.200
I don't think Michael would ever let her go.
我觉得迈克尔永远不会放她走。

402
00:16:32.420 --> 00:16:36.200
I just want to say, Pam, you don't have to worry because Michael thinks you're his personal secretary.
帕姆，我只想说，你不用担心，因为迈克尔把你当成他的私人秘书。

403
00:16:36.680 --> 00:16:37.080
Yeah.
没错。

404
00:16:37.300 --> 00:16:40.440
So even if you got that phone system, you know what it would mean?
所以就算你装了那套电话系统，你知道这意味着什么吗？

405
00:16:40.440 --> 00:16:42.100
She'd probably have to spend more time with Michael.
她可能得花更多时间陪迈克尔。

406
00:16:42.100 --> 00:16:45.260
You wouldn't be as busy, so he'd be like, Pam, come in my office.
你没那么忙的话，他就会说：帕姆，来我办公室。

407
00:16:45.580 --> 00:16:46.120
It's true.
确实如此。

408
00:16:46.580 --> 00:16:51.360
I have to say, I appreciate when a person answers the phone when I call a business.
我得说，我挺喜欢打商务电话时有人接听的感觉。

409
00:16:51.620 --> 00:16:52.040
Me too.
我也是。

410
00:16:52.720 --> 00:16:54.500
I wouldn't like that new phone system.
我可不喜欢那套新电话系统。

411
00:16:54.700 --> 00:16:55.780
I like to get a human.
我喜欢真人接听。

412
00:16:56.060 --> 00:16:56.560
I do too.
我也一样。

413
00:16:56.580 --> 00:16:57.380
I'm chatty.
我这人话多。

414
00:16:57.620 --> 00:17:02.960
Well, I want you to know at 49 seconds, there are a few messages taped to Pam's desk.
我想让你们知道，在49秒的时候，帕姆的桌上贴着几张便条。

415
00:17:03.940 --> 00:17:05.640
I saw the same thing.
我也看到了。

416
00:17:05.740 --> 00:17:06.160
You did?
你也看到了？

417
00:17:06.320 --> 00:17:06.640
Okay.
好吧。

418
00:17:06.940 --> 00:17:08.440
I want to know who Nick is.
我想知道尼克是谁。

419
00:17:09.220 --> 00:17:09.800
Oh, yeah.
哦，对。

420
00:17:09.940 --> 00:17:10.920
There's, like, a message.
上面好像有个留言。

421
00:17:10.920 --> 00:17:15.240
On a Penn Star Post-it note, which, by the way, Penn Star was a bank branch in Pennsylvania.
写在Penn Star的便利贴上，顺便说一下，Penn Star是宾夕法尼亚州的一家银行分行。

422
00:17:15.580 --> 00:17:16.640
Love those details.
我喜欢这些细节。

423
00:17:17.640 --> 00:17:19.560
Nick in office all day.
尼克整天都在办公室。

424
00:17:19.760 --> 00:17:20.120
Yeah.
没错。

425
00:17:20.300 --> 00:17:21.140
That's what the note said.
便条上就是这么写的。

426
00:17:21.400 --> 00:17:22.500
I mean, who is Nick?
我是说，尼克到底是谁？

427
00:17:22.960 --> 00:17:24.700
Well, I know who Nick will be.
嗯，我知道尼克会是谁。

428
00:17:25.540 --> 00:17:28.120
Nick will be our IT guy.
尼克会是我们的IT人员。

429
00:17:28.420 --> 00:17:29.140
Nick will be?
尼克会是？

430
00:17:30.100 --> 00:17:33.780
No, Nick will be our IT guy.
不，尼克会是我们的IT人员。

431
00:17:34.060 --> 00:17:34.540
I know.
我知道。

432
00:17:34.640 --> 00:17:35.040
I'm sorry.
抱歉。

433
00:17:35.240 --> 00:17:36.340
That just made me laugh.
刚才那话把我逗笑了。

434
00:17:36.720 --> 00:17:40.920
Okay, so we don't know who Nick is, but someday in the future, we're going to have an IT guy
好吧，所以我们不知道现在的尼克是谁，但未来某天，我们会有一个IT人员

435
00:17:40.920 --> 00:17:41.440
named Nick.
名叫尼克。

436
00:17:41.600 --> 00:17:41.820
Yes.
没错。

437
00:17:41.820 --> 00:17:44.560
Also, Jenna, was that your grocery list?
还有，珍娜，那是你的购物清单吗？

438
00:17:44.660 --> 00:17:46.120
It was my grocery liSt.
那是我的购物清单。

439
00:17:46.120 --> 00:17:47.740
I know you're getting green tea.
我知道你要买绿茶。

440
00:17:48.060 --> 00:17:50.480
And pomegranate seeds and pine nuts.
还有石榴籽和松子。

441
00:17:50.720 --> 00:17:52.300
What were you, what's happening?
你当时是怎么了，发生什么事了？

442
00:17:52.940 --> 00:17:58.320
Okay, there was the salad I really liked at the time, and it had pomegranate seeds and pine nuts in it.
好吧，当时我特别喜欢吃一种沙拉，里面就有石榴籽和松子。

443
00:17:58.540 --> 00:18:02.300
When I saw that sticky note, I was like, oh my gosh, I should make that salad again.
看到那张便利贴时，我就想，天哪，我应该再做一次那个沙拉。

444
00:18:02.300 --> 00:18:03.040
I loved it.
我超爱那个。

445
00:18:03.160 --> 00:18:04.680
I thought I recognized your handwriting.
我当时就觉得认出了你的笔迹。

446
00:18:04.860 --> 00:18:07.120
I was like, that's Jenna's grocery liSt.
我就想，那是珍娜的购物清单。

447
00:18:07.120 --> 00:18:07.800
It was.
确实是。

448
00:18:08.040 --> 00:18:13.460
Did you also notice there is a photo of me and John on my desk?
你有没有注意到我桌上还有一张我和约翰的照片？

449
00:18:13.460 --> 00:18:14.560
We're standing up.
我们站着的那张。

450
00:18:15.060 --> 00:18:18.100
This was our engagement photo.
那是我们的订婚照。

451
00:18:18.700 --> 00:18:19.220
Yeah.
是啊。

452
00:18:19.520 --> 00:18:21.420
We did this special photo shoot.
我们拍了这组特别的照片。

453
00:18:21.480 --> 00:18:25.740
It was the day that we shot at Jim's parents' house when he's showing me around.
那天是在吉姆父母家拍的，当时他正带我参观。

454
00:18:25.860 --> 00:18:29.280
We brought this extra set of clothes, and we posed in the backyard.
我们带了一套额外的衣服，在后院摆了姿势拍照。

455
00:18:29.760 --> 00:18:31.600
Jim has one on his desk, too.
吉姆的桌上也放了一张。

456
00:18:31.780 --> 00:18:34.640
He does, but on his desk, I'm sitting on his lap.
确实，不过在他桌上那张里，我坐在他腿上。

457
00:18:34.820 --> 00:18:36.380
Right, and on yours, you're standing.
没错，而你那张里，你是站着的。

458
00:18:36.560 --> 00:18:36.840
Yes.
是的。

459
00:18:38.000 --> 00:18:43.040
So this was, I think, they went out for this Valentine's Day episode, our engagement photos.
所以我想，这应该是他们情人节那集里用的订婚照。

460
00:18:44.240 --> 00:18:46.000
Jim's going to come to Pam's rescue.
吉姆要去救帕姆了。

461
00:18:46.380 --> 00:18:47.740
He's like, Michael Scott here.
他就像是迈克尔·斯科特。

462
00:18:47.940 --> 00:18:50.620
And then this next bit was so funny.
接下来的那段戏太搞笑了。

463
00:18:50.940 --> 00:18:53.300
And Jenna, you were so excited to be part of it.
珍娜，你当时特别兴奋能参与其中。

464
00:18:53.420 --> 00:18:54.860
I remember you were, like, so excited.
我记得你当时特别激动。

465
00:18:55.180 --> 00:18:57.720
Because, you know, Michael walks out, and it's like, hey.
因为你知道，迈克尔走出来，就像是，嘿。

466
00:18:57.900 --> 00:18:59.240
And Jim is like, Jimbo.
然后吉姆说，吉姆博。

467
00:18:59.780 --> 00:19:02.900
And instead of Michael being like, what are you talking about?
迈克尔没有问你在说什么。

468
00:19:03.040 --> 00:19:05.440
He's instantly like, ooh, what are we doing?
他立刻就说，噢，我们要玩什么梗？

469
00:19:05.880 --> 00:19:06.560
We're doing a bit.
我们要演一段戏。

470
00:19:07.120 --> 00:19:08.300
I'm so excited.
我太兴奋了。

471
00:19:08.640 --> 00:19:10.720
And then all of a sudden, everyone's Fonzie.
然后突然间，大家都变成了方兹。

472
00:19:11.000 --> 00:19:11.840
I know.
我知道。

473
00:19:12.060 --> 00:19:13.340
It was really fun.
真的很有趣。

474
00:19:13.600 --> 00:19:16.320
We were laughing on the day when we shot that.
拍摄那天我们一直在笑。

475
00:19:16.440 --> 00:19:17.740
It was so fun to do those.
拍那些戏真的太好玩了。

476
00:19:18.340 --> 00:19:24.920
I feel like I should let you know that the phone tech rep was played by Rob Brownstein.
我觉得我应该告诉你，那个电话技术代表是由罗布·布朗斯坦饰演的。

477
00:19:25.320 --> 00:19:26.640
He looked familiar to me.
我觉得他看起来很眼熟。

478
00:19:26.640 --> 00:19:28.100
Well, he's been on Monk.
嗯，他演过《神探阿蒙》。

479
00:19:28.220 --> 00:19:28.580
Oh!
噢！

480
00:19:28.880 --> 00:19:29.320
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

481
00:19:29.680 --> 00:19:30.040
Ah!
啊！

482
00:19:30.200 --> 00:19:34.140
He was also on the short-lived Law & Order Los Angeles.
他还演过短命的《法律与秩序：洛杉矶》。

483
00:19:34.580 --> 00:19:34.960
Oh.
噢。

484
00:19:35.300 --> 00:19:38.060
He's been on Breaking Bad and on Mad Men.
他演过《绝命毒师》和《广告狂人》。

485
00:19:38.520 --> 00:19:39.420
But, lady.
但是，女士。

486
00:19:39.740 --> 00:19:40.140
What?
什么？

487
00:19:40.400 --> 00:19:41.940
His latest movie.
他最新的电影。

488
00:19:42.220 --> 00:19:42.480
Yeah.
嗯。

489
00:19:42.700 --> 00:19:44.220
Which has not come out yet.
还没上映呢。

490
00:19:44.460 --> 00:19:45.160
Oh, no.
噢，不。

491
00:19:45.340 --> 00:19:45.900
No, wait, wait, wait.
不，等等，等等。

492
00:19:45.920 --> 00:19:46.620
Is it John Wick?
是《疾速追杀》吗？

493
00:19:47.060 --> 00:19:47.580
No.
不是。

494
00:19:47.800 --> 00:19:47.960
Oh.
噢。

495
00:19:48.860 --> 00:19:51.460
It's called Hummingbird.
叫《蜂鸟》。

496
00:19:51.700 --> 00:19:52.220
Oh!
噢！

497
00:19:53.040 --> 00:19:54.260
I'll go see it.
我会去看的。

498
00:19:54.440 --> 00:19:55.740
It's a sci-fi movie.
那是一部科幻电影。

499
00:19:55.960 --> 00:19:56.860
Listen to the tagline.
听听这句宣传语。

500
00:19:56.920 --> 00:19:57.400
I'm in.
我加入。

501
00:19:57.400 --> 00:20:04.420
When beloved telepathic superhero Hummingbird, also known as Lola Laxman, is left for dead
