是的。

658
00:26:32.760 --> 00:26:33.760
There wasn't.
并没有。

659
00:26:33.820 --> 00:26:36.520
Except that it clearly says they don't move into Michael's office.
除了剧本明确写着他们不会走进迈克尔的办公室。

660
00:26:36.680 --> 00:26:37.760
They stay at Jim's desk.
他们待在吉姆的桌子旁。

661
00:26:37.880 --> 00:26:41.620
So I think that feels like something that John and Steve probably found in the moment.
所以我认为这感觉像是约翰和史蒂夫当时即兴想出来的。

662
00:26:41.760 --> 00:26:42.600
It's very funny.
非常有趣。

663
00:26:42.600 --> 00:26:43.560
A hundred percent.
百分之百。

664
00:26:43.820 --> 00:26:46.440
And I feel like those guys, you know, we've talked about this a lot.
我觉得他们俩，你知道，我们讨论过很多次了。

665
00:26:46.560 --> 00:26:49.440
By this time, everyone knew their characters so well.
到了这个时候，每个人都对自己扮演的角色非常了解了。

666
00:26:49.620 --> 00:26:55.140
So those tops and bottoms of a scene, you could kind of play around a little bit and it looked
所以对于场景的开头和结尾，你可以稍微自由发挥一下，看起来

667
00:26:55.140 --> 00:26:56.400
like them just having fun.
就像他们只是在玩闹一样。

668
00:26:57.060 --> 00:26:59.260
It's time to talk about Dwight.
是时候聊聊德怀特了。

669
00:27:00.840 --> 00:27:02.480
I feel like Dwight...
我觉得德怀特……

670
00:27:03.780 --> 00:27:04.800
How do I say this?
我该怎么说呢？

671
00:27:04.800 --> 00:27:09.480
I feel like this episode really shows so much of who Dwight is.
我觉得这一集真的展现了很多德怀特的本质。

672
00:27:09.960 --> 00:27:15.440
There's deleted scenes where he talks about the blood mobile being a vampire magnet after dark.
有删减片段是他谈到献血车在天黑后会吸引吸血鬼。

673
00:27:15.820 --> 00:27:18.380
He's ready for anything and everything, you know?
他随时准备应对任何事情，你知道吗？

674
00:27:19.160 --> 00:27:19.620
Yes.
是的。

675
00:27:19.820 --> 00:27:23.320
And he has a lot of stuff to share about how his body can do things.
而且他有很多关于他身体能做到什么程度的事情要分享。

676
00:27:23.780 --> 00:27:24.340
Yes.
是的。

677
00:27:24.660 --> 00:27:29.080
The nurse is trying to take blood, but she can't find a vein.
护士试图抽血，但找不到静脉。

678
00:27:29.640 --> 00:27:30.760
Well, you know why?
嗯，你知道为什么吗？

679
00:27:31.040 --> 00:27:32.300
He's hidden it from her.
他把静脉藏起来不让她看见。

680
00:27:33.020 --> 00:27:35.660
And when he's ready, he's going to pop it on out for her.
等他准备好了，他就会把它弹出来给她抽。

681
00:27:35.920 --> 00:27:36.060
Yeah.
是的。

682
00:27:36.340 --> 00:27:42.440
Then he has a talking head where he tells us he can also retract his penis up into himself.
然后他有一个采访镜头，告诉我们他还能把阴茎缩进体内。

683
00:27:42.680 --> 00:27:42.880
Yeah.
是的。

684
00:27:43.020 --> 00:27:47.220
He says, I train my major blood vessels to retract into my body on command.
他说，我训练我的主要血管听从指令缩进体内。

685
00:27:47.640 --> 00:27:50.360
Also, I can retract my penis up into itself.
此外，我还能把阴茎缩进体内。

686
00:27:50.760 --> 00:27:52.660
We had a fan question from Robin T.
我们收到了罗宾·T的一位粉丝提问。

687
00:27:52.920 --> 00:27:53.940
Robin, go.
罗宾，请说。

688
00:27:54.520 --> 00:27:58.900
Dwight's lines about retracting his blood vessels and penis is one of my
德怀特关于缩回血管和阴茎的台词是我

689
00:27:58.900 --> 00:28:00.760
favorite quotes from the entire show.
整部剧中最喜欢的台词之一。

690
00:28:00.920 --> 00:28:05.240
It is so absolutely absurd and hilarious and so very Dwight.
这绝对荒谬又搞笑，而且非常有德怀特的风格。

691
00:28:05.380 --> 00:28:08.120
I want to know everything about this line.
我想知道关于这句台词的一切。

692
00:28:08.360 --> 00:28:09.880
Was it scripted?
这是剧本写的吗？

693
00:28:10.240 --> 00:28:12.000
How hard was it to get through?
拍的时候忍住不笑有多难？

694
00:28:12.560 --> 00:28:16.680
I'll tell you, it was scripted, but this was an alternate talking head.
我告诉你，这是剧本写的，但这是备选的采访镜头。

695
00:28:16.780 --> 00:28:19.220
This is not the one that appeared in our shooting draft.
这不是我们拍摄初稿中出现的那一个。

696
00:28:19.400 --> 00:28:24.840
So, I wasn't there when they shot it, but I have to imagine it was very difficult to get through.
所以，他们拍摄时我不在场，但我能想象这一定很难拍完。

697
00:28:25.380 --> 00:28:28.040
Well, it's Michael's turn to give blood, guys.
好了，轮到迈克尔献血了，伙计们。

698
00:28:28.040 --> 00:28:30.060
Wow, that's a big needle, he says.
哇，那针头真大，他说。

699
00:28:30.320 --> 00:28:31.680
Are you squeamish around needles?
你对针头感到害怕吗？

700
00:28:32.440 --> 00:28:33.480
I can give blood.
我可以献血。

701
00:28:33.480 --> 00:28:37.040
I don't get faint or anything, but I don't like to watch it.
我倒不会晕倒什么的，但我确实不喜欢看。

702
00:28:37.360 --> 00:28:37.660
Yeah.
是啊。

703
00:28:37.720 --> 00:28:39.380
I don't like to see the needle go in my arm.
我不喜欢看针扎进我胳膊里。

704
00:28:39.380 --> 00:28:44.340
I don't like to see the bag fill up, but I don't like it faint or weird around blood.
我不喜欢看血袋装满，但我对血也不会感到头晕或不适。

705
00:28:44.700 --> 00:28:45.240
Yeah, yeah.
是啊，是啊。

706
00:28:45.240 --> 00:28:47.780
If someone's bleeding, it doesn't make me faint.
如果有人流血，我不会晕倒。

707
00:28:48.000 --> 00:28:48.720
Yeah, same, same.
没错，我也是。

708
00:28:48.900 --> 00:28:49.120
Okay.
好吧。

709
00:28:49.700 --> 00:28:51.760
Michael, on the other hand, is very nervous.
另一方面，迈克尔非常紧张。

710
00:28:51.760 --> 00:28:57.860
But luckily, there's a lovely young woman also giving blood, and they start joking around.
但幸运的是，还有一位可爱的年轻女士也在献血，他们开始开起玩笑来。

711
00:28:58.320 --> 00:28:58.860
Yes.
是的。

712
00:28:59.360 --> 00:29:02.100
We asked Katie about this scene.
我们问了凯蒂关于这场戏的事。

713
00:29:02.280 --> 00:29:10.820
I wanted to know, did she do any research into the process of giving blood and all of that?
我想知道，她有没有对献血的过程之类的做过研究？

714
00:29:10.820 --> 00:29:12.200
And here's what she had to say.
以下是她的回答。

715
00:29:12.200 --> 00:29:29.640
I didn't do any research for this role, but I didn't need to because my character was just nervous and pleasant, and I didn't have to dig super deep to access those emotions.
我没有为这个角色做任何研究，因为没必要，我的角色只是表现得紧张又和善，我不需要深入挖掘就能体会到那种情绪。

716
00:29:29.640 --> 00:29:46.260
But the funny, I do have a very funny anecdote about being nervous, or my character being nervous, is that my first line was me just laughing nervously and saying, I'm so sorry,
但有趣的是，关于紧张，或者说我的角色表现出的紧张，我有一个非常有趣的轶事，我的第一句台词就是紧张地笑着说，我很抱歉，

717
00:29:46.420 --> 00:29:47.360
I'm so nervous.
我太紧张了。

718
00:29:48.100 --> 00:29:56.540
And Steve kept cutting, and he would be like, oh, no, it's okay, we'll go again, we'll go again.
史蒂夫一直喊停，他会说，噢，不，没关系，我们再来一次，再来一次。

719
00:29:56.660 --> 00:30:00.100
And finally, I was just like, I think it's my line.
最后，我只好说，我觉得那就是我的台词。

720
00:30:00.100 --> 00:30:03.320
I think that's what I'm supposed to say.
我想我本来就该那么说。

721
00:30:04.040 --> 00:30:05.860
But that has always made me laugh.
但这件事一直让我觉得很好笑。

722
00:30:05.940 --> 00:30:09.140
And of course, yes, I was thrilled to work with Steve.
当然，能和史蒂夫合作我非常激动。

723
00:30:09.140 --> 00:30:18.920
To get that, to get the show was its own triumph, but then to have my scene be with him was just like, I was over the moon.
能得到这个角色本身就是一种胜利，但能和他演对手戏，我简直高兴坏了。

724
00:30:20.340 --> 00:30:25.200
I love that story about Steve, because he was such a caretaker like that.
我喜欢那个关于史蒂夫的故事，因为他就是那样一个会照顾人的人。

725
00:30:25.340 --> 00:30:31.100
He would want our guest actors to feel really comfortable, and he'd be like, oh, no, it's okay, we'll start again.
他希望客串演员能感到真正舒适，他会说，噢，不，没关系，我们重新开始。

726
00:30:31.240 --> 00:30:32.360
We'll wait until you're comfortable.
我们等你准备好了再说。

727
00:30:32.700 --> 00:30:34.480
I was like, no, it's actually my line.
我当时就想，不，那其实是我的台词。

728
00:30:35.180 --> 00:30:41.280
I would also be relieved if the first time I ever had to be in a scene with Steve, I got to just laugh nervously and say I was nervous.
如果我第一次和史蒂夫演对手戏，我也能紧张地笑笑说我很紧张，我也会感到如释重负。

729
00:30:41.400 --> 00:30:41.720
Yes.
是的。

730
00:30:42.120 --> 00:30:43.800
Because it would be so truthful.
因为那会非常真实。

731
00:30:44.120 --> 00:30:45.400
Such an honest moment.
真是个诚实的瞬间。

732
00:30:45.660 --> 00:30:45.780
Yeah.
是啊。

733
00:30:46.180 --> 00:30:48.000
There's a third person in this scene.
这场戏里还有第三个人。

734
00:30:48.220 --> 00:30:49.240
It's the nurse.
就是护士。

735
00:30:49.460 --> 00:30:50.540
She was great.
她演得很好。

736
00:30:50.840 --> 00:30:54.860
I wondered if she was a real bloodmobile nurse, since that was a real bloodmobile.
我很好奇她是不是真正的献血车护士，因为那确实是一辆真正的献血车。

737
00:30:55.040 --> 00:30:58.460
Yeah, and she seemed kind of no-nonsense, like very comfortable there.
是啊，她看起来很干练，在那儿待得很自在。

738
00:30:58.700 --> 00:31:00.440
Well, she was, in fact, an actress.
嗯，事实上，她是一位演员。

739
00:31:00.780 --> 00:31:02.240
Her name is Julie Ramallah.
她叫朱莉·拉马拉。

740
00:31:02.760 --> 00:31:04.220
She has not been on Monk.
她没演过《神探阿蒙》。

741
00:31:04.480 --> 00:31:05.500
Or Law and Order.
也没演过《法律与秩序》。

742
00:31:05.660 --> 00:31:11.000
But she was on several episodes of The Young and the Restless, as well as many movies and TV shows.
但她出演过几集《年轻和骚动不安的一族》，以及许多电影和电视剧。

743
00:31:11.220 --> 00:31:13.920
Well, Michael's going to make the mistake of looking at his blood bag.
嗯，迈克尔犯了个错误，他盯着自己的血袋看。

744
00:31:14.220 --> 00:31:15.420
He freaks out a little.
他有点吓坏了。

745
00:31:15.700 --> 00:31:17.300
And he says to her, tell me stories.
他对她说，给我讲讲故事。

746
00:31:17.440 --> 00:31:17.820
Say something.
说点什么吧。

747
00:31:18.020 --> 00:31:18.600
Distract me.
分散一下我的注意力。

748
00:31:19.080 --> 00:31:20.640
And she says he's cute.
她说他很可爱。

749
00:31:21.100 --> 00:31:21.600
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

750
00:31:21.780 --> 00:31:23.360
And he's, I think, so happy.
我想他当时一定很高兴。

751
00:31:23.560 --> 00:31:28.800
And then he shares that he didn't eat for three days because he was so nervous about giving blood.
然后他分享说，因为太紧张不敢献血，他已经三天没吃东西了。

752
00:31:28.940 --> 00:31:30.100
And he passes out.
结果他晕倒了。

753
00:31:30.480 --> 00:31:30.920
Yes.
没错。

754
00:31:30.920 --> 00:31:32.120
We had a fan question.
我们收到一个粉丝提问。

755
00:31:32.480 --> 00:31:38.680
Many, many people wanted to know, how do we do these scenes of people giving blood?
很多人都想知道，我们是怎么拍那些献血场景的？

756
00:31:38.920 --> 00:31:41.580
Some people wanted to know, did they actually give blood?
有些人想知道，他们是真的献血了吗？

757
00:31:41.760 --> 00:31:42.200
No.
没有。

758
00:31:42.440 --> 00:31:43.240
Oh, my goodness.
天哪。

759
00:31:43.360 --> 00:31:43.720
No.
没有。

760
00:31:44.180 --> 00:31:44.440
You know.
你知道的。

761
00:31:44.440 --> 00:31:45.400
Not in the episode.
剧集里没有。

762
00:31:45.720 --> 00:31:48.720
Well, yes, the next day, but not while we were filming.
嗯，是的，那是第二天，但不是在拍摄的时候。

763
00:31:49.560 --> 00:31:53.500
The next day with trained professionals and not actors pretending to take blood.
第二天是在专业人员的指导下，而不是让演员假装抽血。

764
00:31:53.640 --> 00:31:53.940
Correct.
没错。

765
00:31:54.680 --> 00:31:57.820
I found out how they make fakie blood.
我打听到了他们是怎么制作假血的。

766
00:31:58.500 --> 00:31:58.980
Oh.
哦。

767
00:31:59.480 --> 00:32:00.880
Thanks to Randy Cordray.
多亏了Randy Cordray。

768
00:32:01.120 --> 00:32:02.120
How do they do it?
他们是怎么做的？

769
00:32:02.380 --> 00:32:02.760
All right.
好吧。

770
00:32:02.960 --> 00:32:09.300
It's a combination of water, food coloring, and you're not going to believe it.
它是用水、食用色素混合而成的，你绝对想不到还有什么。

771
00:32:10.360 --> 00:32:11.280
One more thing.
还有一样东西。

772
00:32:11.940 --> 00:32:12.480
Wait, wait, wait.
等等，等等，等等。

773
00:32:14.980 --> 00:32:15.980
You'll never guess.
你绝对猜不到。

774
00:32:16.260 --> 00:32:16.780
Wait, wait, wait.
等等，等等，等等。

775
00:32:16.820 --> 00:32:17.640
I want to try to guess.
我想试着猜一下。

776
00:32:17.940 --> 00:32:18.980
You can eat it.
它是可以吃的。

777
00:32:19.220 --> 00:32:20.680
I thought you could eat it.
我刚才就想说可以吃。

778
00:32:20.740 --> 00:32:21.980
I was going to say like Jell-O.
我本来想说是像果冻那样的东西。

779
00:32:22.720 --> 00:32:23.500
Nestle's quick.
雀巢速溶巧克力粉。

780
00:32:23.940 --> 00:32:24.500
Oh.
哦。

781
00:32:25.040 --> 00:32:25.560
Yeah.
是的。

782
00:32:26.000 --> 00:32:27.660
That thickens it a little, I guess.
我想那能让它稍微浓稠一点。

783
00:32:27.800 --> 00:32:27.980
Yeah.
是的。

784
00:32:28.500 --> 00:32:33.080
So our blood was all made by our special effects team led by Ron Nary.
所以我们的血都是由Ron Nary领导的特效团队制作的。

785
00:32:33.440 --> 00:32:35.140
Had to make fakie blood that day.
那天得制作假血。

786
00:32:35.300 --> 00:32:35.460
Fakie blood.
假血。

787
00:32:35.720 --> 00:32:41.900
Well, I thought the reveal of Hank when Michael comes to was one of the best moments.
我觉得Michael醒来时看到Hank的那一幕是全剧最精彩的时刻之一。

788
00:32:42.100 --> 00:32:43.440
I laughed so hard.
我笑得好大声。

789
00:32:43.600 --> 00:32:44.620
It was so perfect.
真是太完美了。

790
00:32:44.820 --> 00:32:45.460
It was so perfect.
真是太完美了。

791
00:32:45.460 --> 00:32:46.900
And then he calls the nurse a waitress.
然后他管护士叫服务员。

792
00:32:47.020 --> 00:32:48.320
He's like so out of it.
他当时神志不清。

793
00:32:48.540 --> 00:32:50.140
And he finds her glove.
他还发现了她的手套。

794
00:32:50.340 --> 00:32:51.340
He does.
确实。

795
00:32:51.340 --> 00:32:51.480
He does.
确实。

796
00:32:51.880 --> 00:32:55.140
And this starts his whole mission to find her.
这开启了他寻找她的整个任务。

797
00:32:55.360 --> 00:32:56.760
To return the glove.
为了归还手套。

798
00:32:56.940 --> 00:32:57.220
Yeah.
是的。

799
00:32:57.360 --> 00:32:58.680
Like Cinderella's slipper.
就像灰姑娘的水晶鞋一样。

800
00:32:58.840 --> 00:32:59.220
I know.
我知道。

801
00:32:59.300 --> 00:33:00.100
It's really cute.
这真的很可爱。

802
00:33:00.660 --> 00:33:06.220
We have one more clip from Katie where she just shares her memories of her time on the show.
我们还有一段凯蒂的视频，她分享了自己在剧组时的回忆。

803
00:33:06.380 --> 00:33:09.380
I asked her, anything stick out to you?
我问她，有什么特别让你印象深刻的事吗？

804
00:33:09.580 --> 00:33:11.960
And Angela, wait until you hear what she says.
安吉拉，等着听听她怎么说。

805
00:33:12.100 --> 00:33:12.720
Oh, I can't wait.
哦，我等不及了。

806
00:33:13.880 --> 00:33:27.560
I don't remember a ton of details about my time on set, except for that you guys were on your last day of like a very, very, very long cycle of shooting.
我不记得在片场时的太多细节了，只记得当时你们正处于一个非常、非常、非常漫长的拍摄周期的最后一天。

807
00:33:27.560 --> 00:33:36.380
And everyone was just dead, tired, and just ready for a hiatus.
每个人都累得半死，只想赶紧放假。

808
00:33:36.760 --> 00:33:39.940
So that is what I remember.
这就是我记得的。

809
00:33:40.100 --> 00:33:41.120
But they were lovely.
但大家都很可爱。

810
00:33:41.520 --> 00:33:43.100
Everyone was great.
每个人都很棒。

811
00:33:43.480 --> 00:33:52.160
But just like the talk was all about how this hiatus was just so needed.
只是大家都在谈论这次假期是多么迫切需要。

812
00:33:52.760 --> 00:33:53.820
So that's what I remember.
所以我记得的就是这些。

813
00:33:55.140 --> 00:33:58.240
That and that you guys moved so quickly.
还有就是你们的动作非常快。

814
00:33:58.580 --> 00:33:59.920
It was like the fasteSt.
简直快得惊人。

815
00:34:00.020 --> 00:34:02.180
I don't even know if I got lunch that day.
我甚至不知道那天我有没有吃午饭。

816
00:34:02.300 --> 00:34:03.140
Like I showed up.
我到了片场。

817
00:34:03.420 --> 00:34:04.520
I did my scene.
演了我的戏份。

818
00:34:04.620 --> 00:34:07.580
And I'm pretty sure you guys banged me out.
我敢肯定你们很快就把我打发走了。

819
00:34:07.660 --> 00:34:09.180
And I didn't even get a free lunch.
我连顿免费午餐都没混上。

820
00:34:10.280 --> 00:34:10.760
All right.
好吧。

821
00:34:10.760 --> 00:34:20.020
This was, remember early on, we had to do 18 episodes in a row so that we could create that hiatus for Steve to go do a movie?
还记得早期吗？我们不得不连续拍摄18集，这样才能给史蒂夫腾出假期去拍电影？

822
00:34:20.220 --> 00:34:20.380
Yeah.
是的。

823
00:34:20.740 --> 00:34:22.420
This was that 18th episode.
这就是那第18集。

824
00:34:22.680 --> 00:34:24.400
We were so wiped.
我们当时累坏了。

825
00:34:24.760 --> 00:34:25.060
Yep.
没错。

826
00:34:25.400 --> 00:34:27.940
18 weeks of 12 to 14 hour days.
18周，每天工作12到14个小时。

827
00:34:28.180 --> 00:34:28.340
Yeah.
是啊。

828
00:34:28.780 --> 00:34:37.420
And you guys, you know when you have that stretch of work where you leave work and it's dark out and then you come back to work and it's still dark out?
你们知道那种感觉吗，就是当你有一段工作期，下班时天已经黑了，第二天来上班时天还是黑的？

829
00:34:37.420 --> 00:34:38.140
You know what I mean?
你们懂我的意思吗？

830
00:34:38.180 --> 00:34:39.260
Because you're there so early.
因为你来得太早了。

831
00:34:39.660 --> 00:34:44.400
And you're just like, and you sort of all look at each other and joke and be like, see you in a few hours.
大家看着彼此开玩笑说，几个小时后再见。

832
00:34:44.800 --> 00:34:45.880
There's a whole thing now.
现在有个专门的词。

833
00:34:46.000 --> 00:34:46.880
It's called clopening.
叫“关开”（clopening）。

834
00:34:47.800 --> 00:34:48.160
Clopening?
关开？

835
00:34:48.520 --> 00:34:48.880
Clopening.
关开。

836
00:34:49.100 --> 00:34:58.080
And it's a lot of people who work in the service industry or in the food industry where you have to close the restaurant and then like a few hours later you have to open it.
很多在服务业或餐饮业工作的人都会这样，你得负责关店，然后几个小时后又得回来开店。

837
00:34:58.200 --> 00:34:58.440
Yeah.
是的。

838
00:34:58.720 --> 00:34:59.080
Clopening.
关开。

839
00:34:59.460 --> 00:34:59.820
Clopening.
关开。

840
00:35:00.020 --> 00:35:01.600
Well, we were in the clopening phase.
好吧，我们当时就处于“关开”阶段。

841
00:35:01.660 --> 00:35:02.240
We were.
确实是。

842
00:35:02.240 --> 00:35:09.060
That is hilarious to me because I do remember like when we would wrap after a big stretch like that, I would get like a cold.
这对我来说太搞笑了，因为我确实记得，每当经历那样一段高强度工作后杀青，我就会感冒。

843
00:35:09.200 --> 00:35:09.840
I would get sick.
我会生病。

844
00:35:09.980 --> 00:35:10.880
We talked about that.
我们聊过这个。

845
00:35:10.980 --> 00:35:11.160
Yeah.
是的。

846
00:35:11.320 --> 00:35:14.220
Right now we were about to all get sick.
当时我们都快要病倒了。

847
00:35:14.360 --> 00:35:14.600
Yeah.
是啊。

848
00:35:14.800 --> 00:35:15.100
Basically.
基本上是这样。

849
00:35:15.560 --> 00:35:18.660
And Katie clocked it and has remembered it all these years later.
凯蒂注意到了这一点，并且在多年后的今天依然记得。

850
00:35:18.780 --> 00:35:19.960
That's how tired we were.
我们当时就是累成那样。

851
00:35:20.080 --> 00:35:21.000
We were so tired.
我们当时太累了。

852
00:35:21.420 --> 00:35:23.600
Next up is a scene I'm dying to talk about.
接下来要讲的这一幕，我迫不及待想聊聊。

853
00:35:23.820 --> 00:35:24.940
It's in the conference room.
场景是在会议室。

854
00:35:25.560 --> 00:35:28.780
Kelly and Meredith are decorating for the Lonely Hearts party.
凯莉和梅雷迪斯正在为“孤独之心”派对做装饰。

855
00:35:28.780 --> 00:35:32.900
Kelly, is this a good time to talk about how Meredith is wearing the vest again?
凯莉，现在适合聊聊梅雷迪斯又穿那件背心的事吗？

856
00:35:33.080 --> 00:35:33.560
Yes.
是的。

857
00:35:33.660 --> 00:35:34.400
The sweater veSt.
那件毛线背心。

858
00:35:34.420 --> 00:35:39.840
It is making its second appearance in the series pretty quickly because it was just in the duel.
它在剧里这么快就第二次出场了，因为刚才在决斗那集才穿过。

859
00:35:40.260 --> 00:35:40.660
Yes.
没错。

860
00:35:40.800 --> 00:35:44.820
This is the vest that I wore to a press event with John Krasinski.
这件背心是我和约翰·卡拉辛斯基一起参加媒体活动时穿的那件。

861
00:35:45.280 --> 00:35:48.120
And by the way, it was not Betsy Johnson.
顺便说一下，那不是贝齐·约翰逊的牌子。

862
00:35:48.360 --> 00:35:49.340
It was Nanette Lepore.
是娜内特·莱波雷的。

863
00:35:49.980 --> 00:35:50.540
Fancy.
真高级。

864
00:35:50.880 --> 00:35:54.480
And Meredith loves it clearly and is wearing it again.
显然梅雷迪斯很喜欢它，所以又穿上了。

865
00:35:54.760 --> 00:35:57.220
They were really, I think, rubbing it in my face.
我觉得她们真的是在故意气我。

866
00:35:58.200 --> 00:35:59.700
I take it personally.
我个人对此很介意。

867
00:35:59.780 --> 00:36:00.520
I'm kidding.
开个玩笑。

868
00:36:00.820 --> 00:36:04.840
Well, there's something happening now that I, as an actor, am super jealous of.
好吧，现在发生了一件事，作为演员的我超级嫉妒。

869
00:36:05.140 --> 00:36:09.600
Because Jim and Pam are going to go to frickin' lunch with Bob and Phyllis.
因为吉姆和帕姆要去跟鲍勃和菲利斯吃午饭了。

870
00:36:09.940 --> 00:36:12.820
Jenna, I would have loved to have been there.
珍娜，我真希望能在那儿。

871
00:36:12.900 --> 00:36:14.400
That looked like so much fun.
看起来太好玩了。

872
00:36:14.400 --> 00:36:15.520
And I love it.
我真的很喜欢。

873
00:36:15.600 --> 00:36:19.640
It's like the thing we talk about when random characters get thrown together.
就像我们常说的，当一些不常交集的角色被凑在一起时。

874
00:36:19.980 --> 00:36:21.020
What's going to happen?
会发生什么呢？

875
00:36:21.180 --> 00:36:22.000
What's the chemistry?
会有什么样的化学反应？

876
00:36:22.260 --> 00:36:23.860
I lived for every scene.
我期待着每一场戏。

877
00:36:23.860 --> 00:36:26.340
And there was so much more in the script.
剧本里原本还有更多内容。

878
00:36:26.500 --> 00:36:28.320
And there's more in the deleted scenes.
删减片段里也有更多内容。

879
00:36:29.140 --> 00:36:31.120
Phyllis and I were so excited for this storyline.
菲利斯和我对这条故事线感到非常兴奋。

880
00:36:31.500 --> 00:36:33.120
We're the two St. Louis gals.
我们俩都是圣路易斯来的姑娘。

881
00:36:33.400 --> 00:36:33.820
Yeah.
是啊。

882
00:36:34.040 --> 00:36:36.740
And we got to have this whole day of shooting together.
我们能一起拍一整天的戏。

883
00:36:36.920 --> 00:36:38.080
We got to talk about bowling.
我们聊了保龄球。

884
00:36:38.700 --> 00:36:39.140
Yes.
没错。

885
00:36:40.120 --> 00:36:43.440
We had a fan question from Joe S.
我们收到了乔·S的一位粉丝提问。

886
00:36:43.680 --> 00:36:47.580
Where were the restaurant scenes for the double date filmed?
双重约会的餐厅戏是在哪里拍的？

887
00:36:47.920 --> 00:36:49.080
I will tell you.
我来告诉你。

888
00:36:49.440 --> 00:36:53.900
They were filmed at a real restaurant called Barsak Brasier.
是在一家叫Barsak Brasier的真实餐厅拍的。

889
00:36:54.100 --> 00:36:56.560
It was on Lancashire Boulevard in North Hollywood.
它位于北好莱坞的兰开夏大道上。

890
00:36:56.860 --> 00:37:02.840
We filled the restaurant with background performers who were pretending to be servers and diners.
我们找了些群众演员填满餐厅，让他们假装成服务员和食客。

891
00:37:03.080 --> 00:37:05.040
We had the restaurant for half a day.
我们包下了那家餐厅半天。

892
00:37:05.300 --> 00:37:07.980
It is no longer in business, but that's where we were.
它现在已经倒闭了，但那就是我们当时拍摄的地方。

893
00:37:07.980 --> 00:37:09.720
And we ate their real food.
而且我们还吃了他们真正的食物。

894
00:37:09.880 --> 00:37:15.480
Well, if you look at the tables, there you're going to see Jim's bouquet of flowers to Pam on every table.
如果你仔细看桌子，会发现每张桌子上都有吉姆送给帕姆的那束花。

895
00:37:15.660 --> 00:37:17.500
I'll do a side-by-side in our stories.
我会把对比图发到我们的快拍里。

896
00:37:18.160 --> 00:37:21.100
And I want to ask you, Jenna, about the scene with the bowling.
珍娜，我想问你关于打保龄球的那场戏。

897
00:37:21.440 --> 00:37:21.720
Okay.
好的。

898
00:37:22.060 --> 00:37:22.400
All right.
没问题。

899
00:37:22.560 --> 00:37:25.900
So Bob says, everyone here who's bowled a 280, please raise your hand.
鲍勃说，在座各位有谁打过280分的，请举手。

900
00:37:26.260 --> 00:37:27.820
And you guys are like super impressed.
然后你们看起来超级佩服。

901
00:37:28.120 --> 00:37:28.340
Yeah.
是啊。

902
00:37:28.620 --> 00:37:30.100
What's the highest bowling number?
保龄球的最高分是多少？

903
00:37:30.380 --> 00:37:30.780
300.
300分。

904
00:37:31.200 --> 00:37:32.240
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

905
00:37:32.520 --> 00:37:32.720
Yeah.
是啊。

906
00:37:32.720 --> 00:37:33.460
That's a big deal.
那可是个大数字。

907
00:37:33.600 --> 00:37:34.700
I don't know a lot about bowling.
我对保龄球了解不多。

908
00:37:34.840 --> 00:37:35.720
I don't know much about bowling.
我对保龄球不太了解。

909
00:37:35.720 --> 00:37:38.340
300 is if you get a strike in every frame.
300分意味着你每一局都打出了全中。

910
00:37:38.680 --> 00:37:39.200
Wowzers.
哇哦。

911
00:37:39.960 --> 00:37:40.320
Okay.
好吧。

912
00:37:40.640 --> 00:37:49.900
Well, there was a whole other storyline where clearly the writers wanted Jim and Pam to be impressed by how cool Bob and Phyllis were.
其实还有另一条故事线，编剧显然是想让吉姆和帕姆觉得鲍勃和菲利斯很酷。

913
00:37:50.080 --> 00:37:54.920
There was a whole other scene where you guys talk about how you went to Dave Matthews' band.
还有另一场戏，你们聊到去看戴夫·马修斯乐队演出的事。

914
00:37:55.040 --> 00:37:55.440
Yes.
没错。

915
00:37:55.620 --> 00:37:57.040
I remember shooting it.
我记得拍过那场戏。

916
00:37:57.040 --> 00:38:01.360
And they had great seats in that Phyllis like went backstage and all this stuff.
他们当时的位置特别好，菲利斯甚至还去了后台之类的。

917
00:38:01.560 --> 00:38:01.720
Yeah.
是啊。

918
00:38:01.960 --> 00:38:02.960
We're like, oh, my gosh.
我们当时就想，天哪。

919
00:38:03.160 --> 00:38:04.480
Bob and Phyllis are kind of cool.
鲍勃和菲利斯还挺酷的。

920
00:38:05.880 --> 00:38:08.680
And then they excused themselves to the restroom.
然后他们就借口去洗手间了。

921
00:38:09.140 --> 00:38:16.660
We got some mail from Emily Y, who really appreciated the callback from Phyllis' wedding about Phyllis being a good bowler.
我们收到了艾米丽·Y的来信，她很喜欢菲利斯婚礼上关于菲利斯是个保龄球高手的那个梗。

922
00:38:16.920 --> 00:38:17.540
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

923
00:38:17.680 --> 00:38:19.160
I also enjoyed that.
我也很喜欢那个梗。

924
00:38:19.160 --> 00:38:25.460
If you guys remember, Bob has a speech at their reception where he refers to Phyllis as, quote, a hell of a bowler.
如果你们还记得的话，鲍勃在婚宴上致辞时，称呼菲利斯为“超级保龄球高手”。

925
00:38:25.460 --> 00:38:26.160
That's right.
没错。

926
00:38:26.700 --> 00:38:30.600
I think we should take a break before we go to Michael's Lonely Hearts party.
我觉得在进入迈克尔的“孤独之心”派对之前，我们应该先休息一下。

927
00:38:31.140 --> 00:38:31.820
I do, too.
我也这么觉得。

928
00:38:31.920 --> 00:38:32.480
Is that okay?
可以吗？

929
00:38:32.800 --> 00:38:33.940
I think we should, too.
我也觉得应该休息一下。

930
00:38:34.520 --> 00:38:36.920
Before we go to break, I just want to say one thing.
在休息之前，我只想说一件事。

931
00:38:37.060 --> 00:38:37.500
What is it?
什么事？

932
00:38:37.560 --> 00:38:44.120
That I love that Bob says, I don't know how you work with that one jackass and then that new jackass and that other jackass.
我特别喜欢鲍勃说的那句：“我不知道你怎么能跟那个混蛋，还有那个新来的混蛋，以及另一个混蛋一起工作。”

933
00:38:45.240 --> 00:38:48.160
Yeah, and Phyllis is like, he means Michael, Dwight, and Andy.
是啊，然后菲利斯说，他指的是迈克尔、德怀特和安迪。

934
00:38:48.340 --> 00:38:49.980
And Jim's like, oh, I knew who he was talking about.
吉姆就说，噢，我知道他在说谁。

935
00:38:49.980 --> 00:38:50.030
I knew.
我知道。

936
00:38:50.060 --> 00:38:50.280
I knew.
我当然知道。

937
00:38:51.900 --> 00:38:52.700
Oh, that's great.
噢，太棒了。

938
00:38:52.980 --> 00:38:53.660
Let's go to break.
我们休息一下吧。

939
00:38:53.660 --> 00:39:16.720
We are back, and since I shared about my hot feet today, I thought I would also share about another wardrobe malfunction that I discovered during my bathroom break,
我们回来了，既然我分享了今天脚发烫的事，我想再分享一下我在上厕所时发现的另一个穿衣事故，

940
00:39:16.900 --> 00:39:19.460
which is that I put my underwear on inside out today.
那就是我今天把内裤穿反了。

941
00:39:19.740 --> 00:39:20.220
Oh.
噢。

942
00:39:20.840 --> 00:39:22.520
I'm having that day, everybody.
大家，我今天真是倒霉透了。

943
00:39:23.380 --> 00:39:26.160
I think I look really put together today.
我觉得我今天看起来穿得很得体。

944
00:39:26.540 --> 00:39:27.300
Do I?
是吗？

945
00:39:27.520 --> 00:39:28.620
Or is it?
还是说并没有？

946
00:39:28.740 --> 00:39:29.160
No.
没有。

947
00:39:29.520 --> 00:39:30.020
You know?
你知道吧？

948
00:39:30.240 --> 00:39:31.280
You didn't say yes.
你刚才没说“是”。

949
00:39:31.580 --> 00:39:35.320
In fact, you've got to look on your face like, how do I say this?
事实上，你脸上的表情就像是在说，我该怎么开口呢？

950
00:39:35.600 --> 00:39:36.380
You know what?
你知道吗？

951
00:39:36.560 --> 00:39:37.060
You know why?
你知道为什么吗？

952
00:39:37.200 --> 00:39:38.200
I don't want you to move.
我不希望你动。

953
00:39:38.360 --> 00:39:38.780
Don't move.
别动。

954
00:39:38.960 --> 00:39:39.380
Oh, no.
噢，不。

955
00:39:39.520 --> 00:39:39.920
Don't move.
别动。

956
00:39:40.000 --> 00:39:42.640
I just want to take a picture of your hair, and then I'm going to answer.
我只是想拍张你头发的照片，然后我就回答你。

957
00:39:45.620 --> 00:39:45.980
Okay.
好的。

958
00:39:46.240 --> 00:39:50.040
Now, you just said, I feel pretty put together today.
刚才你说，我觉得今天自己打扮得挺得体的。

959
00:39:50.040 --> 00:39:51.460
Now, I want you to look at this.
现在，我想让你看看这个。

960
00:39:53.700 --> 00:39:54.060
Okay.
好的。

961
00:39:54.880 --> 00:39:55.440
Okay.
好的。

962
00:39:55.760 --> 00:39:58.860
Now, your outfit, lady, it's all happening.
你的这身装扮，女士，简直太棒了。

963
00:39:59.020 --> 00:40:02.240
You have your little shirt and pants and your fancy sneakers.
你穿着小衬衫、裤子，还有那双时髦的运动鞋。

964
00:40:02.900 --> 00:40:04.560
I like your look today.
我很喜欢你今天的造型。

965
00:40:05.080 --> 00:40:05.540
Good.
很好。

966
00:40:05.920 --> 00:40:06.360
Okay.
好的。

967
00:40:06.600 --> 00:40:06.780
Okay.
好的。

968
00:40:07.060 --> 00:40:07.460
All right.
行吧。

969
00:40:07.600 --> 00:40:10.040
Let's go to the Lonely Hearts party.
我们去参加“寂寞芳心”派对吧。

970
00:40:10.360 --> 00:40:11.220
Let's do.
走吧。

971
00:40:11.380 --> 00:40:17.260
Because Michael wants to go around and have everyone tell their worst relationship story.
因为迈克尔想让大家轮流讲出自己最糟糕的感情经历。

972
00:40:17.500 --> 00:40:19.660
Michael has this way of like, oh, you don't feel good?
迈克尔总有那种感觉，噢，你感觉不好吗？

973
00:40:19.660 --> 00:40:21.100
I want you to feel worse.
那我要让你感觉更糟。

974
00:40:21.100 --> 00:40:21.880
Yeah.
是啊。

975
00:40:22.280 --> 00:40:26.280
I think he thinks this is going to be, I don't know, bonding, cathartic.
我想他觉得这会是一种，我不知道，增进感情、宣泄情绪的方式。

976
00:40:27.440 --> 00:40:31.020
Well, you guys, we had to sit in a circle facing each other.
好吧，伙计们，我们得围成一圈面对面坐着。

977
